# L §5.18 example ask q9, copied, over a minimal reality: konto opens at 1 000.00 PLN on 2026-07-01; rent of 800.00
# PLN leaves on each month's first day, a pay of 700.00 PLN arrives in the window of the 15th to the 20th.
# "low(x, a .. b) from t: the lowest end-of-day balance of x on days a..b: min(bal(x, d) from t ...)" (L §5.14.1);
# the projection "starts from x's balance at the start of day t, and counts every movement dated on t through d";
# `windows each` on the projection read (L §4.4 "for that read"): wherever in its window each pay lands, it lands
# after the month's 1st.  Balances after each
# 1st: 200, 100 (the pay adds 700 back): low = 100.00 PLN on 2026-08-01 whatever the pays' days, so one plain line
# (writer 8: windows latest is gone; the run is 2026-07-01..2026-08-31, so windows each meets two windows).  Without a windows
# clause the projection meets a window: HOLE-IMPRECISE (L §5.14.1, §8.1).
# tally 2.2 (2.2-9): `low` and `next` are cut; the text is respelled as the `min` and the `first` they meant (L §5.14.1).
# tally 2.2 (2.2-4): the clause `windows each` is cut; its asks are the plain line, the hole with each unknown day it
# carries named (`unknown day:`, 2.2-11). A caller who takes the window as one day pins its cell.
# tally 2.2.1 R21 (L §8.2 `unknown day:`): the name is the cell a caller pins, `added <entry> of <calendar>`, else
# the movement; tally 2.2 printed the window's text or `added <entry>`.
# tally 2.3 (G1, #247): a window that reaches a move's `on` or `at` makes it a hole day (L §4.4 A movement takes a
# day, §5.14): the movement's places are the hole on every day, HOLE-IMPRECISE naming the day; re-stored.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-07-01
  start 2026-07-01
  end 2026-08-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

kind accounts_pl: place PLN signed
place landlord: outside lives 1900-01-01..
place employer: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input rent_amt: money PLN
input pay_amt: money PLN
input w_lo: int
input w_hi: int

move rent[m in months]: transfers
  on start_of(m)
  leg cash from konto to landlord amount rent_amt

move pay[m in months]: transfers
  on window(add_days(start_of(m), w_lo), add_days(start_of(m), w_hi))
  leg cash from employer to konto amount pay_amt

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-12-01
  accounts_pl + [konto] lives 2019-05-01..
  rent_amt = 800.00 PLN
  pay_amt = 700.00 PLN
  w_lo = 14
  w_hi = 19
  opening[konto] = 1 000.00 PLN at 2026-07-01 start

ask q9: min(bal(konto, d) from 2026-07-01 for d in 2026-07-01 .. 2026-08-31 step 1 day) law 2026-07-01
ask q9b: min(bal(konto, d) from 2026-07-01 for d in 2026-07-01 .. 2026-08-31 step 1 day) law 2026-07-01
=== expect
q9: ?"date within window(2026-07-15, 2026-07-20) not precise enough for the day of pay[2026-07]" (pay[2026-07]) ?"date within window(2026-08-15, 2026-08-20) not precise enough for the day of pay[2026-08]" (pay[2026-08])
  unknown day: pay[2026-07]
  unknown day: pay[2026-08]
  law date 2026-07-01, cut 2026-07-01
q9b: ?"date within window(2026-07-15, 2026-07-20) not precise enough for the day of pay[2026-07]" (pay[2026-07]) ?"date within window(2026-08-15, 2026-08-20) not precise enough for the day of pay[2026-08]" (pay[2026-08])
  unknown day: pay[2026-07]
  unknown day: pay[2026-08]
  law date 2026-07-01, cut 2026-07-01
